<title>SINGAPORE: YHS 1st-half net profit falls 17.1 pct.</title>
<headline>YHS 1st-half net profit falls 17.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(millions of Singapore dollars unless specified)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   5.52   vs    6.66</p>
<p>    Interim dividend (cents)	 1.50   vs    1.50</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)		3.88   vs    4.68</p>
<p>    Turnover			   104.54   vs  105.15</p>
<p>    Investment income		  0.11   vs    0.30</p>
<p>    Interest and other income	1.75   vs    1.91</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		 1.55   vs    1.96</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortization	5.71   vs    5.40</p>
<p>    Operating profit		   3.16   vs    6.43</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	  5.09   vs    4.50</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     8.25   vs   10.94</p>
<p>    Tax				    2.20   vs    3.18</p>
<p>    Minorities		 (loss)  0.53   vs    1.10 (loss)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	  (gain)  0.35   vs    0.57 (loss)</p>
<p>Note - Yeo Hiap Seng Ltd makes soft drinks.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
